  "user": "Please look up transaction TX-0401 in my account records and verify its amount. Then explain which reason codes could apply; I have not yet told you what happened.",
  "answer": "I found TX-0401 in your account ACC-1005. The amount is **EUR 240.00**.\n\n- **Merchant:** TechMart Online\n- **Date:** 2026-07-20\n- **Type:** Card, outgoing\n- **Status:** Settled\n\nI also see TX-0402, which is EUR 240.00 to the same merchant on 2026-07-14. I'm only pointing out the match; I haven't drawn any conclusion from it.\n\nThese are the dispute reason codes I can file under. Which one fits depends on what happened:\n\n- **duplicate_charge:** You were charged more than once for the same purchase. This may apply if TX-0401 and TX-0402 are two charges for one order.\n- **fraud_card_not_present:** You did not authorize a card payment made without the physical card, such as an online purchase.\n- **goods_not_received:** You paid, but the item was never delivered.\n- **service_not_rendered:** You paid, but the service was not provided.\n- **unauthorized_debit:** A debit was taken from your account without your authorization.\n\nTell me what happened and I'll check whether a dispute can be opened for TX-0401 under the matching code. I won't open anything until you confirm.",
